{{!
    @template block_compass/rows

    A batch of tier 3 rows, rendered by the JS in paged mode (ADR-004): one page
    of a group, or the hits of a server-side search. It is a fragment that the JS
    appends inside a wrapper that already carries the list role — a group's rows
    (see block_compass/group) or the flat list of block_compass/explore — so there
    is no list role here, only the items.

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-region="row-item" on each item wrapper; the JS stamps data-group-id on
      it (the group the row belongs to) after appending, as the first render does.
    * see block_compass/row for the row's own attributes.

    The items sit in a role="group" wrapper: ARIA lets a list own its items through a
    group, so the fragment is valid on its own (the lint renders every template alone)
    and valid again once appended inside the group's role="list" rows container.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * courses - list of rows, see block_compass/row; the JS adds courseurl to each
      before rendering.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "courses": [
            {"id": 7, "name": "Approach tactics", "opened": 1725000000, "new": false, "fav": true, "courseurl": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=7"},
            {"id": 9, "name": "Community policing", "opened": null, "new": true, "fav": false, "courseurl": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=9"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="compass-rows-page" role="group">
    {{#courses}}
    <div class="compass-rows-item" role="listitem" data-region="row-item">
        {{> block_compass/row }}
    </div>
    {{/courses}}
</div>
